  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Between the Modules",
      "items": [
        "Green arrows are Integration Events and Snapshots, written to the Outbox in the publishing Unit of Work's commit and delivered to each subscription; no Module references another Module.",
        "Inventory and Billing reference Catalog's Contracts and never Catalog: Inventory receives ProductCreatedV1, ProductCreatedV2 and ProductSnapshotV1, Billing ProductCreatedV1 under its own subscription.",
        "Billing schedules ExpireQuote as a delayed command; Inventory declares ReconcileStock as a recurring command for the system Actor inventory.stock-reconciler."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The two Hosts",
      "items": [
        "With ConnectionStrings:broker, ModularMonolith.Host composes Catalog and Billing under the service name modular-monolith, and Inventory.Host composes Inventory under the service name inventory; what Catalog publishes then reaches Inventory over RabbitMQ.",
        "Inventory.Host composes ModularMonolith.ServiceDefaults; ModularMonolith.Host does not.",
        "ModularMonolith.ReverseProxy composes the service defaults and PouryaKit.ReverseProxy, runs no Operation, and routes every path to ModularMonolith.Host, whose liveness probe its settings turn off.",
        "ModularMonolith.ServiceDefaults references EF Core Relational for its readiness check, OpenTelemetry, service discovery, Serilog, PouryaKit.Web and PouryaKit.Observability.",
        "ModularMonolith.AppHost, an Aspire AppHost, runs both Hosts as processes on PouryaKit.Aspire's containers, giving each the connection strings its composition reads: with the broker, ModularMonolith.Host leaves Inventory to Inventory.Host.",
        "ModularMonolith.Host also composes PouryaKit.Reporting.Module, a Kit package no template packs, with its one report kind, SalesReports, and stores the reports in an S3 bucket."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "The templates",
      "items": [
        "PouryaKit.Templates keeps no copy of the business code: it packs the sample Modules' code, the service defaults recipes and two files of ModularMonolith.Host when the package is packed.",
        "Each template's Host, Reverse proxy, project files and smoke test are the template's own; the monolith takes Catalog without Modularity."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
